  "findings": "The current IRO catalogue and regulations establish 60 EC in each year. Year two has eleven required 5 EC courses and a choice of Contemporary Political Philosophy or Rational Choice Theory. The current catalogue uses 6442HASRBY for Academic Skills: Research Design where the annex lists 6442HASRDY. Year three has a 10 EC seminar, 20 EC Bachelor Project and 30 EC of approved open study. Political Leadership is one seminar example. The seminar requires the first year, and the project also requires 40 EC from year two including Research Design, Statistics II and Qualitative Research Methods. The project combines subject instruction with an individual thesis based on original research. The module assigns 40% to the subject assignments and 60% to the thesis, which must pass separately. The elective space needs approval; a research internship may count for 15 EC and has separate entry requirements.",
  "authority": "2026–2027 English annex Appendix 2 §§2.2 and 2.5–2.20 controls credit and progression; annual product and exact module records control current titles, Research Design code, and current seminar and thesis detail. The overview chart uses an older distribution of first-year skills; exact current catalogue and annex agree on the 5 EC Introduction to Political Science and 7 EC Actors in World Politics and Academic Skills 2. Information meetings and careers support add no scheduled credits."
}
